From: Florent Kermarrec <florent@enjoy-digital.fr>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 10:40:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/22] test: extend AXISRAM coverage with burst-type and width
 sweeps

The single test_axi_sram smoke test only exercised one burst length
(INCR-16) at one data width (32) on one base address. Catching real
AXI2AXILite/AXIBurst2Beat bugs needs a wider sweep. Lift the AXI4
driver helpers (axi_aw_send / axi_w_send / axi_b_recv / axi_ar_send
/ axi_r_recv_one and the higher-level write_single / read_single /
write_burst / read_burst) out of test_axi_sram to module level so
all the AXISRAM tests share them, and add four focused tests:

  - test_axi_sram_burst_lengths: INCR with len = 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32,
    64, 128, 256.  Covers both the pathological 1-beat case (degenerate
    burst behaving like a single beat) and the AXI4 maximum (256 beats
    in a single transaction).
  - test_axi_sram_wrap_burst: WRAP-{2,4,8,16}.  Verifies that data
    written via a WRAP burst lands at the right *physical* addresses
    (we cross-check by single-beat reads from each address in the
    block), and that a subsequent WRAP read returns the same beats in
    WRAP order.  This is the burst type CPU caches typically issue for
    line refills.
  - test_axi_sram_back_to_back: 40 alternating random write/read
    bursts against a software model of the SRAM, lengths drawn from
    {1, 2, 4, 8, 16}.  Catches FSM-state-leak bugs in AXI2AXILite
    (state not reset between bursts, AW/AR contention, etc.) that a
    single transaction can't expose.
  - test_axi_sram_64bit: same shape as test_axi_sram but on a 64-bit
    AXI bus with size=3 (8 bytes/beat).  Exercises the wider data /
    strobe paths and the AXILiteSRAM internal Memory port being
    instantiated at width 64.

All 5 AXISRAM tests pass; full test_axi.py / test_axi_lite.py /
test_wishbone.py suites green (68/68 + 25 subtests).

